  Read more



### 4. CONTROL CONSIDERATIONS

- Whether each production AI application has a named business owner, an appro=
ved purpose, documented action permissions and a reassessment trigger when it=
s autonomy or customer impact changes? (Risk, Technology)
- Whether transaction-capable agents operate within customer consent, payment=
 limits and approval boundaries, with records distinguishing what the custome=
r authorised from what the agent inferred during execution? (Payments, Legal)
- Whether reported interaction-resolution rates exclude abandoned calls, repe=
at contacts and unresolved complaints, and whether customer outcomes are meas=
ured separately from automated completion of the underlying workflow? (Custom=
er Operations, Conduct)
- Whether self-hosted models have documented weight provenance, licence terms=
, patch responsibilities and data-flow maps covering logs, monitoring service=
s, administrative access and any external support connections? (Technology, S=
ecurity)
- Whether model-routing decisions compare total operating costs, including in=
frastructure, validation, human review and remediation, rather than treating =
a reduction in token expenditure as an equivalent financial saving? (Finance,=
 Procurement)
- Whether AI-assisted reconciliation preserves original records, identifies u=
ncertain matches and records human overrides, allowing operations teams to re=
construct how an exception was resolved after processing has finished? (Marke=
ts Operations, Audit)
- Whether employee training is connected to approved tools, role-specific per=
missions and demonstrated competence, with attendance figures distinguished f=
rom evidence that staff can recognise errors and escalate exceptions? (Human =
Resources, Compliance)
- Whether fallback arrangements have been tested when an AI service fails, lo=
ses access to source documents or produces unsupported answers, including the=
 capacity of human teams to absorb demand? (Operational Resilience, Business =
Continuity)

